    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d698">

                <pb facs="0812" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg802"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.67/11–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-18T12:00:00+08:00">November 18,
                            1948—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received November 18—1:50 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2457. Arrangements being made for Koval and Bernhardt depart Shanghai November 24
                    via <hi rendition="#italic">Smolny</hi> to Vladivostok and onward travel to
                    Dairen. In view uncertain conditions, Department’s authorization requested for
                    Consulate General advance total $2,500 to Koval and Bernhardt for travel
                    expenses and per diem while at Vladivostok.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 2457; repeated Moscow 35, Dairen 90, pouched Nanking 1857.
                    Department pass Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cabot</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
